// HTTP/2 framing, RFC 9113 §4 and §6: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9113
//
// The nine-octet header and all ten frame types, with padding stripped on the way
// in and re-emitted on the way out, and the connection preface of §3.4. An
// unrecognised frame is kept verbatim (§4.1) so a reader can forward or ignore it
// rather than fail.
//
// `Conn` is a whole connection on top of the frames, after python-hyper h2: the
// stream states of §5.1, flow control of §6.9, settings, field validation of §8,
// and the header compression of `moonhttp/hpack`, still without a socket.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonvar/fixed",
  "moonbitstack/moonhttp/header",
  "moonbitstack/moonhttp/hpack",
}
